{"content":"Fixed in `lib/src/cli/agent_cli.dart` — adopted the suggested one-liner almost verbatim.

The aborted branch now notes the downgraded opt-in before printing the detach summary:

```dart
if (terminalStopReason == StopReason.aborted) {
  if (waitForJobs) {
    io.writeln(
      'aborted: skipping --wait-for-jobs (run shutdown) — '
      'background jobs keep running',
    );
  }
  await _waiting.printHeadlessDetachSummary();
}
```

The note goes through `io` (so it lands on the terminal/stderr channel, not the HEP/stream-json stdout frame channel), keeping the explicit `--wait-for-jobs` override observable on the record.

TDD: new test in `test/cli/agent_cli_waiting_integration_test.dart` — an abortable headless run started with `waitForJobs: true`, interrupted mid-turn: exits 130 and the captured output contains `skipping --wait-for-jobs`. Failed before the change, passes after.
